            <ArticleTitle>Prostate-specific antigen doubling time and response to cabazitaxel in a hormone-resistant metastatic prostate cancer patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>420-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7555/JBR.28.20130148</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer, who received prior treatment with docetaxel and was then given cabazitaxel as salvage therapy. The patient was monitored by prostate-specific antigen doubling time and prostate-specific antigen absolute value. The prostate-specific antigen doubling time was found to be a good response predictor in the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
